import SymmetricSubgroupAsymptotics.External.CFSG.Certificates.Mathieu24.Certificates.SteinerSystem

/-!
# The final stabilizer certificate

This file proves that a degree-24 permutation that preserves the candidate
`S(5,8,24)` block set and fixes the seven base points `23,22,0,1,2,5,3` is
the identity.

As for `M23` (and unlike `M22`), the automorphism group of the design is
the Mathieu group itself, so pure forced block propagation pins every
remaining point with no parity argument: a block with five known point
images maps to the unique block through the images, and each unknown point
is caught either in the intersection of two pinned blocks or as the last
unknown point of a pinned block.

All propagation steps are Lean-checked `decide` certificates generated by
`scripts/build_m24.py`.
-/

